architecture interaction-grammar
  canonical_name InteractionGrammar
  family surface
  domain Surface / Native interaction grammar
  layer compiler
  semantic_question How can a studied market interaction grammar become reusable native surface composition without importing a donor product's ontology, backend, or data?
  purpose Native closed grammar catalog and subject-binding compiler. It contains twenty researched donor-informed interaction shapes, emits AddressPlane descriptors for active bindings, and hands each to the deployed InteractionGrammarCompiler consumer. CreatorChannel and MediaLibrary bindings are derived from current native owner rows; public CreatorChannel candidates can invoke the existing ChannelSurfaceCompiler through the worker after that recheck.
  maturity measured
  owns InteractionGrammarCatalog
  owns InteractionGrammarBinding
  consumes AddressClosure
  publishes CandidateAdvertisement
  publishes SurfacePlan
  publishes PendingExactOwnerSurfaceComposition
  publishes ChannelSurfaceProjection
  node_types InteractionGrammar
  node_types InteractionGrammarBinding
  node_types SurfaceCompositionIR
  edge_types binds_interaction_grammar
  edge_types advertises_interaction_grammar
  edge_types compiles_pending_surface_composition
  edge_types projects_public_channel_surface
  internal_calculus grammar basis x subject/institution/owner binding x forwarding coordinates -> candidate -> native consumer recheck -> pending exact-owner composition; CreatorChannel(public) -> existing Channel surface compiler -> content-addressed derived projection | retired binding omitted
  invariant a grammar catalog entry is a reusable interaction shape, not a subject, user, message, media identity, relationship, right, authority, provider, payment, external protocol enactment or effect
  invariant only an active binding carrying a concrete subject and owner reference emits an AddressPlane candidate; retirement atomically removes the old grammar population from the derived index
  invariant a binding owner must carry the catalogued native owner-family prefix, so a Community grammar cannot be advertised as an Offer, Finance or invented owner population
  invariant a candidate carries a verifier and lowerer reference but never an owner result; deterministic mask selection remains eligible_for_further_consideration only
  invariant AddressPlane always dispatches InteractionGrammarCompiler:surface, which reopens the canonical binding. A CreatorChannel-derived public binding additionally reopens current channel/publication rows and invokes the existing Channel surface compiler; all other target lowerers remain recorded only as pending_exact_owner.
  invariant source-derived bindings retain source kind/ref and the worker refuses them when the current CreatorChannel published-kind or MediaLibrary active-membership predicate is absent; this is an owner-state recheck, not actor-specific visibility, playback, delivery, or proof.
  invariant all runtime grammar coordinates use compact address terms; pretty donor and owner identifiers remain boundary references and never hot forwarding terms
  forbidden_inference a donor grammar -> copied donor code, donor backend, protocol compatibility, a donor user or an entitlement
  forbidden_inference a grammar binding -> an executed exact verifier, a lawful disclosure, admission, delivery, payment, commitment or effect
  source_path cmd/BonfyreInteractionGrammar/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreInteractionGrammar/tests/interaction_grammar_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreLoweringWorkers/src/main.c
  source_path schemas/control/address-advertisement.cue
  source_path research/interaction-grammar-market-2026.md
  witness cmd/BonfyreInteractionGrammar/tests/interaction_grammar_test.sh proves an exact 20-grammar native catalog, refuses a cross-family owner binding, compiles and forwards all 20 grammar IDs, routes a 20-binding FactDelta batch through durable handoffs, ignores previously handled files, rechecks canonical bindings, derives YouTube/TikTok/Spotify bindings from live CreatorChannel/MediaLibrary rows, rechecks their current source predicates, invokes the existing public Channel surface compiler for both CreatorChannel grammars, emits content-addressed pending exact-owner compositions, and atomically removes a retired binding from the derived population
  source_lineage current official product documentation recorded in research/interaction-grammar-market-2026.md
  known_gap Community, Workspace, Social, Correspondence, Knowledge, Artifact, Board, Commerce and Protocol target lowerers still require their own exact-owner recheck and consumption path. MediaLibrary source state is rechecked, but actor-specific catalog/playback remains on its authenticated owner path; it is not a rendered Listen surface here.
